From 6a5e417887d51f2f8d9a5077a8b66f7803fbf0fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:03:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 115/116] Keep the attribute tables when none of their inputs
 changed

Every geometry update rebuilt the attribute requests, layout comparison,
object attribute requests, attribute map and kernel object offsets by
walking every geometry and object, also on pose-only updates where none of
their inputs changed (20-25 ms per object or light edit on 380k objects,
and 35 ms on a full object table write). When no geometry other than
lights was modified (sockets or attributes; for lights their shaders), no
shader was updated in this scene update, the object update's change list
is valid (no object added, removed, reordered or given another geometry,
and every earlier object update reached a completed geometry update), the
global attribute requests, OSL mode, geometry count and attribute table
sizes are those of the last completed attribute update, no attribute or
primitive buffer is to be reallocated and every changed object still
requests the same attributes, only the changed objects' attribute values
and kernel object offsets are written and copied.

CYCLES_FULL_ATTRIBUTE_TABLES always runs the full update, as a reference.
CYCLES_VERIFY_ATTRIBUTE_TABLES compares every device copy with the host and
the kept tables, map and kernel objects with those of the full update, and
reports a difference as an error.

Rationale: Pose-only edits on large instanced scenes spent 20-45 ms rebuilding attribute requests, maps and offsets that could not have changed.
Contract: Attribute tables, attribute map and kernel objects on every device equal those of the full update (checked by CYCLES_VERIFY_ATTRIBUTE_TABLES); any changed input listed above takes the full update.
Tests: tests/houdini_attribute_tables_kept_smoke.py
